<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Function Notation — evaluating f(a) for a negative input</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Let \(f(x) = {@fx@}\).</p>
<p>Evaluate \(f({@a@})\).</p>
<div>\(f({@a@}) =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Function notation \(f({@a@})\) means the <strong>output</strong> of \(f\) when the <strong>input</strong> is \(x={@a@}\). To evaluate it, replace every \(x\) in the rule by \(({@a@})\), keeping the brackets so that the negative sign travels with the number. Then follow the order of operations: the power first, then the multiplications, then the additions.</p>
\[ f({@a@}) = {@p@}({@a@})^2 + {@q@}({@a@}) + {@r@} = {@p@}\times {@a^2@} + ({@q*a@}) + {@r@} = {@ta@}. \]
<p>Squaring a negative number gives a <strong>positive</strong> result: \(({@a@})^2 = {@a^2@}\), not \({@-a^2@}\). Multiplying the positive coefficient \({@q@}\) by the negative input gives a <strong>negative</strong> result, \({@q*a@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[p : rand_with_prohib(2,6,[]);
q : rand_with_prohib(2,9,[]);
r : rand_with_prohib(1,9,[]);
a : -rand_with_prohib(2,6,[]);          /* always negative, to force careful sign handling */
fx : p*x^2+q*x+r;
ta : subst(x=a,fx);
/* Diagnostics. ta-wrong_sign = 2*p*a^2 >= 16 and ta-wrong_lin = 2*q*a <= -8, so neither can equal ta (or ta+1). */
wrong_sign : -p*a^2+q*a+r;              /* treated (a)^2 as if it kept the negative sign */
wrong_lin : p*a^2-q*a+r;                /* lost the negative sign in the linear term q*a */]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
